Title: Height and Depth in BST
Develop a program that constructs a Binary Search Tree and computes the height of
the tree and the depth of a given node.
Software Used: ‘C’ programming tool (DEV C++)
Theory:
A Binary Search Tree (BST) is a special type of binary tree in which:
Each node has at most two children.The left child contains values less than the parent node.
The right child contains values greater than the parent node.
Height of a Tree:
The height of a binary tree is the number of edges on the longest path from the root node to a leaf
node.
For an empty tree, height = –1 (or sometimes defined as 0).
It can be found recursively by taking the maximum height of left and right subtrees and adding 1.
Depth of a Node:
The depth of a node is the number of edges from the root node to that specific node.
It can be found iteratively by traversing the tree and counting levels until the key is found.


