Algorithm:
Step 1: Start
Step 2: Create a structure node with data, left, and right pointers.
Step 3: Write a function createNode(value) to create a new node with given data.
Step 4: Write an insert() function to insert nodes into BST using the following rule:
• If the tree is empty, create a new node.
• If value < root->data, insert into the left subtree.
• If value > root->data, insert into the right subtree.
Step 5: Write a function height(root)
• If root == NULL, return -1.
• Recursively find height of left and right subtrees.
• Return the greater of the two plus 1.
Step 6: Write a function depth(root, key)
• Initialize d = 0.
• Traverse the tree from root and compare key with root->data.
• If key matches, return d.
• Else move left or right depending on comparison, incrementing d.
• If key not found, return -1.
Step 7: In main() function:



• Accept number of nodes and their values.
• Insert nodes in BST using insert().
• Display height of the tree using height().
• Accept a node value and display its depth using depth().
Step 8: Exit
